after:
Here is the complete example.
```javascript
function addCounters(left, right) {
  return BigInt(left) + BigInt(right);
}
console.log(String(addCounters("9007199254740993", "2")));
try { console.log(2n + 1); } catch (error) { console.log(error.name); }
```
Output:
```text
9007199254740995
TypeError
```
The large sum keeps every digit. The second calculation mixes BigInt and Number, so it fails. `catch` receives the error, and `error.name` gives its name.
